# Dev-only defaults. Vite loads `.env.development` in dev mode and IGNORES it
# for `vite build`, so nothing here can reach a production bundle — which is
# what makes it safe to turn mocks on by default.
#
# The point: `git clone && pnpm install && pnpm dev` works with no backend and
# no setup step. Skipping a setup step was otherwise the most likely first
# mistake, and it failed unhelpfully — `/api/...` hits the dev server, returns
# index.html, and the route shows a definite-failure error that says nothing
# about the missing flag.
#
# Point the app at a real backend by setting VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET and
# VITE_ENABLE_MOCKS=false in `.env.local`, which wins over this file.
VITE_ENABLE_MOCKS=true
